  "response": "<issues>\n- The input parsing reads raw bytes using `sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()` and leaves the face values as byte strings rather than integers. While this happens to work here because `Counter` will just hash the byte strings, it is unidiomatic and strictly bypasses the problem's definition of faces as integers.\n- The inner loop performs two dictionary lookups per matched face (`if face in large_c:` followed by `large_c[face]`). This can be optimized to a single lookup using `large_c.get(face)` to improve performance.\n- The manual index tracking for input parsing can be streamlined and made faster by using an integer iterator with `itertools.islice`.\n</issues>\n<solution>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import islice\n\ndef main():\n    # Read all standard input at once and split by whitespace\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    # Create an iterator over all integers in the input\n    iterator = map(int, input_data)\n    n = next(iterator)\n    \n    dice = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        k = next(iterator)\n        # Use islice to efficiently consume exactly k elements for the current die\n        c = Counter(islice(iterator, k))\n        dice.append((k, c))\n        \n    best = 0.0\n    for i in range(n):\n        ki, ci = dice[i]\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            kj, cj = dice[j]\n            \n            # Always iterate over the die with fewer unique faces\n            if len(ci) > len(cj):\n                small_c, large_c = cj, ci\n            else:\n                small_c, large_c = ci, cj\n                \n            s = 0\n            for face, cnt in small_c.items():\n                # Single dictionary lookup optimization\n                cnt2 = large_c.get(face)\n                if cnt2 is not None:\n                    s += cnt * cnt2\n                    \n            p = s / (ki * kj)\n            if p > best:\n                best = p\n                \n    # Output the result with 15 decimal places of precision\n    print(f\"{best:.15f}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n</solution>",
